{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-222465","model_call":3,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3452"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3452"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_35_292435872#6_734110712","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3452","rank":3,"snippet":"found on women as evidence in criminal prostitution cases against them. It's easy to imagine how this practice might deter sex workers from carrying protection. The United Nations Development Programme published a report last year on <cover>illegal sex work in Asia and the Pacific that highlighted just how damaging the criminalization of sex work can be to women's health. Here's what it said: Criminalization increases vulnerability to HIV by fueling stigma and discrimination, limiting access to HIV and sexual health services, condoms and harm reduction services, and adversely affecting the self-esteem of sex workers and their ability to make informed choices about their health. Prostitution Is Arguably A Victimless Crime While some advocates argue that prostitutes are victims of Johns and pimps, sex work can be a victimless crime if women sell their bodies of their own volition. ( Moreover, it doesn't make sense to arrest sex workers if they are their own \"victims.\")\" , \"start_char\": 3756.000000 , \"title\": \"Why </cover>America Should Legalize Prostitution\" , \"url\": \"https://www.businessinsider.com/why-america-should-legalize-prostitution-2013-11\" }"},"time":10},"model_calls":3,"document_judgments":2,"relevance_3":1,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
