{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-222465","model_call":36,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ prostitution legalization opponents trafficking exploitation violence)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ prostitution legalization opponents trafficking exploitation violence)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_34143540#1_37844194","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3476","rank":1,"snippet":"<cover>Legalization Decriminalization Negative effects of criminalization Health Discrimination and stigma Human rights abuses Poverty Specific populations Male sex workers Transgender sex workers Practical comparison Abolitionist practice Brazil Neo-abolitionist (Nordic) practice Canada France Sweden Legalisation (regulationist) practice Denmark Germany Netherlands Nevada, United States Decriminalisation practice New South Wales, Australia Towards prohibition 1908–1976 Partial decriminalisation and re-criminalisation 1976–1995 Decriminalisation 1995–present New Zealand Washtenaw County, Michigan (United States) See also References Further reading \" , \"segment\": \"The decriminalization of sex work is a controversial topic. Advocates of decriminalization argue that removing the criminal sanctions surrounding sex work creates a safer environment for sex workers, and that it helps fight sex trafficking. Opponents of decriminalization argue that it will not prevent trafficking (or even increase trafficking) and could put sex workers at greater risk. Organizations such as UNAIDS, WHO, Amnesty International, Human Rights Watch, UNFPA, and the medical journal The Lancet have called on states to decriminalize sex work in the global effort to tackle the HIV/AIDS epidemic and ensure sex workers' access to health services. Almost all organisations run by sex workers themselves around the world favour the decriminalisation of sex work, and </cover>"},"time":37},"model_calls":36,"document_judgments":26,"relevance_3":10,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
