{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-222465","model_call":61,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ prostitution disease illegal trafficking)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ prostitution disease illegal trafficking)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_569687760#6_1039249587","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3493","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_569687760#6_1039249587\" , \"end_char\": 5378.000000 , \"headings\": \"Prostitution Prostitution Terminology History In the ancient world Near East Greece Rome Middle Ages Sixteenth century Eighteenth century to present Types Street Escort/Out-call Sex tourism Prostitution and the Internet Religious prostitution Current issues involving prostitution Legality<cover>Prostitution of children Illegal immigration Violence against prostitutes Human trafficking and sexual slavery Disease</cover>Feminism Occurrence Impact on society Notable quotes regarding prostitution Notes References External links Credits \" , \"segment\": \"Within the religion of Canaan, a significant portion of temple prostitutes were male. It was widely used in Sardinia and in some of the Phoenician cultures, usually in honor of the goddess ‘Ashtart. Presumably under the influence of the Phoenicians, this practice was developed in other ports of the Mediterranean Sea, such as Erice ( Sicily ), Locri Epizephiri, Croton, Rossano Vaglio, and Sicca Veneria. Prostitution was common in ancient Israel, despite being tacitly forbidden by Jewish Law. It is recorded in the Bible that a prostitute in Jericho named Rahab assisted Israelite spies with her knowledge of "},"time":181},"model_calls":61,"document_judgments":43,"relevance_3":17,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
